WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.367
How does sunlight become the power in your home?

cue-2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.833
Let's follow the energy, step by step.

cue-3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.900
Solar panels are made of silicon cells.

cue-4
00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:12.733
When sunlight hits them, it knocks electrons loose and creates a direct current.

cue-5
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.600
An inverter converts that direct current into alternating current, the kind your home actually uses.

cue-6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.967
And there is plenty of it.

cue-7
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:25.933
The sunlight reaching Earth in about ninety minutes roughly matches a whole year of global energy use.

cue-8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.600
Extra energy from the afternoon charges a home battery, so the lights stay on after sunset.

cue-9
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.100
Output follows the sun.

cue-10
00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:37.267
It climbs through the morning, peaks around midday, and fades by evening.

cue-11
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:41.767
Every image, clip and diagram here came from one short GPU session.

cue-12
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.300
